  <p style="max-width: 720px; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.97rem; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 32px;">
    Every carpet roll coming off Mohawk's tufting lines was wound to the same 900 yard
    preset, regardless of the style's face weight, stitch density, or pile construction.
    As a manufacturing engineering intern, I spent the summer replacing that single number
    with a geometry-based model and a regression equation that sets a defensible, style-specific
    maximum length for each product family, then validated it with statistical process
    control before it went anywhere near the production floor.
  </p>

  <div class="metric-row">
